# Dev-mode init-data bypass.
#
# Local browser dev only. Works ONLY when:
#   1. Django backend runs with DEBUG=True
#      (DJANGO_DEBUG=True uv run python manage.py runserver)
#   2. Vite runs in dev mode (npm run dev — production builds dead-code-
#      eliminate the bypass branch entirely)
#   3. Both vars below are set
#   4. No real MAX initData is present in window.WebApp (i.e. you're in
#      a plain Chrome tab, not inside the MAX wrapper)
#
# When all four hold, the Mini App injects three headers on every API
# request:
#   X-Dev-Bypass: 1
#   X-Dev-User-Id: <VITE_DEV_BYPASS_USER_ID>
#   X-Dev-Tenant-Slug: <VITE_DEV_BYPASS_TENANT_SLUG>
# The backend (apps/miniapp_api/dev_bypass.py) resolves the BotUser +
# Tenant from these headers, skipping HMAC verification.
#
# SECURITY:
#   - In production builds (npm run build) these headers are NOT injected
#     — the branch is dead-code-eliminated by Vite.
#   - In production backend (DEBUG=False) these headers are IGNORED —
#     the dev_bypass helper exits before reading any header.
#   - DO NOT commit .env.local. It is already in .gitignore.
#
# Bootstrap:
#   After running `python manage.py create_test_master_invite`, run
#   `python manage.py print_master_dev_env <master_id>` once the master
#   is linked (M0 onboarding complete) — it prints the snippet to paste
#   below.

VITE_DEV_BYPASS_USER_ID=
VITE_DEV_BYPASS_TENANT_SLUG=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Support deeplink (#949).
#
# Real MAX support channel URL rendered by the Profile support-entry
# sheets (152-ФЗ export/delete + notification prefs). Optional in dev —
# `npm run dev` falls back to the historical placeholder. REQUIRED for
# `npm run build`: production builds fail fast without it (guard in
# vite.config.ts) so a placeholder can never ship a silent 404.
VITE_SUPPORT_DEEPLINK=
